<item>
            <title>[LU-20532] port ext4-mballoc-dense.patch to newer kernels</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20532</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;tt&gt;ext4-mballoc-dense.patch&lt;/tt&gt; was added in patch &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/50171&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/50171&lt;/a&gt; (&quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10026&quot; title=&quot;Client-side data compression&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-10026&quot;&gt;LU-10026&lt;/a&gt; osd-ldiskfs: use preallocation for dense writes&quot;) for el8.x kernels, but is missing patches for el9, el10, and ubuntu26 servers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This functionality is needed to optimize ldiskfs block allocation for compressed files, which are stored in ldiskfs with a hole after every compressed chunk of data.  This would otherwise cause significant filesystem free space fragmentation if compression is used.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
